<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Points the glow genes at a class that does nothing, so nothing ticks.

       Glowing eyes genes drives its glow from Gene.Tick, which fires once per gene
       per tick for as long as the pawn exists. A Harmony patch can stop that tick
       doing any work but cannot stop it being called, which left a floor of
       thousands of near-empty calls a second whether or not a single pawn was
       glowing. The glow does not need a tick at all - it is a render node now, and
       its trail is laid from the same pass that draws it - so the cheapest fix is
       for their class never to be instantiated.

       Nothing is disabled and nothing is overwritten. Their assembly still loads;
       their gene defs, textures, mote and fleck defs, mod extension and settings
       window all still work and are all still used. geneClass is an ordinary XML
       field, so this is the whole change.

       Applied to the abstract parent because PatchOperations run on raw XML before
       ParentName inheritance is resolved. Pawns from an older save come back
       holding the original class, since saves store a gene's concrete type; those
       are swapped over once on load, in LegacyGeneMigration. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Glowing eyes genes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[@Name="GEG_GeneGlowingEyes"]/geneClass</xpath>
      <value>
        <geneClass>GlowingEyesScaled.Gene_EyeGlow</geneClass>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
